  "_about": "UINTATHERIUM (Eocene North America, 2026-11-08; generator tools/creaturegen/prehistoric/gen.py): a uintathere about 3.9 m long and 1.6 m at the shoulder, some 2 t -- a heavy rhino-like barrel on stout pillar legs, five-toed pad feet (five hoof-nails each); a long low skull with a small brain case, its roof dished between THREE PAIRS of blunt skin-covered bony knobs -- a small pair on the nose tip, a pair before the eyes, the largest at the back of the skull above the ears, leaning out; the bull's long dagger UPPER CANINES hanging past the chin beside the bony downward FLANGE of the lower jaw that guards them; small rhino-like ears, a short tail; grey-brown, near-hairless skin. Every knob, tusk and nail a sharp `horn` faired into the skin; the ears the rhinoceros' cupped `fin` scaled. Coats grey-brown, dun, slate; variant `cow` (smaller, short tusks and knobs)."
